power: supply: sc27xx_fuel_gauge: UMP9620 (UMS9620's PMIC)

The same FGU as the SC2731 with its enable bits at 0x2008/0x2010 and the 4200 mV calibration in bits 15:7 of
its efuse word (Unisoc's 5.4 driver). On these boards "bat-temp" is the NTC's voltage: the battery node's
voltage-temp-table turns it into a temperature. The charger IC has no driver, so the status comes from the
battery current. current_now read a discharge current as a huge positive one (an unsigned subtraction; the
vendor driver casts to s64 first). The ZTE U30 Air's battery under mainline.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
